<title>ITALY: Olivetti shares plunge, suspended in Milan.</title>
<headline>Olivetti shares plunge, suspended in Milan.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in crisis-struck Italian information technology group Olivetti fell 10 percent on the Milan bourse triggering automatic suspension 20 minutes after the start of trade on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Olivetti shares plummeted to a fresh record low of 465 lire per share following news market regulator Consob had demanded answers to 16 points it wanted clarified regarding the group's financial performance.</p>
</text>
